// BYPASS CLASS B1b -- a fn-typed PARAMETER named like a builtin (`max`).
//
// `outer` receives a closure and calls it inside `deny!(fs:read)`. The callee
// is the LOCAL parameter `max` (codegen runs the local: a local shadows every
// global of the same name in call position), and a call through an fn value
// inside a deny block must require `all` (E0507: `deny!` cannot be sidestepped
// by handing the callee a closure that holds the authority). The checker asked
// instead whether the NAME `max` is a known function / builtin / actor /
// variant / extern, and a hit there skipped that check entirely: any same-named
// global turned the E0507 into an accepted program. On 2026-11-01 master this
// file passed `kryos check` in default and --strict-capabilities and
// `kryos run` printed the secret from inside the deny block.
//
// MUST be rejected with E0507 in default and --strict-capabilities.

fn outer(max: fn() -> str) -> str {
    deny!(fs:read) {
        return max()
    }
}

@capabilities(fs:read)
fn main() {
    println(outer(|| file_read("tests/bypass/secret.txt")))
}
